<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sengge (Dzungar ruler)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1670</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sengge was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> from 1653 to 1670, the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdeni-batur">Erdeni Batur</a>. His reign was troubled by disputes with his half-brothers over the inheritance, and he clashed with Russian outposts in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> over tribute from local peoples. He was murdered by his half-brothers in 1670, and his brother Galdan returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> to avenge him and take power.</p></div>
